        "quote": "if (allowed === undefined || !allowed.includes(pressedBy)) {",
        "problem": "No test drives the fail-closed branch of operatorConfirmTool.invoke where the allowed-id list is undefined (config unreadable or no binding), the one branch that makes a remote answer refuse when the allow-list is missing.",
        "impact": "If the `allowed === undefined ||` half is dropped or inverted (for example `allowed !== undefined && !allowed.includes(...)`, or `allowed?.includes(pressedBy) === false`), every existing test still passes while any remote press is accepted whenever the remote config is missing or unreadable. This is the security gate of AC2 and the one place where a refactor turns a refusal into an acceptance without a red test.",
        "suggested_fix": "Add two direct invoke tests in the AC2 block of operator-confirm-tools.test.ts: (1) bind `allowedUserIds: () => undefined`, ask, press remote with pressedBy 42 and a valid token, expect isError and unchanged state (no apply side effect, no confirmation record); (2) bind a tool with no `allowedUserIds` at all and do the same. Assert the refusal text contains 'not on the allowed list' and that the token is spent.",
        "evidence": "operator-confirm-tools.ts line 215 holds the only allow-list check. The tests at operator-confirm-tools.test.ts lines 331-395 all construct the gate with `{ allowedUserIds: () => ALLOWED }`; the review-tools helper `tool()` binds `allowedUserIds: () => [ALLOWED_ID]`. shell.ts line 4224 shows the production binding can return undefined.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "class_scope": {
          "sites": [
            "src/commands/operator-confirm-tools.ts:215 (allowed === undefined fail-closed branch)"
          ],
          "enumeration_method": "keryx ctx rg for 'allowed === undefined' and 'allowedIds === undefined' across src; the branch exists at operator-confirm-tools.ts:215 only (src/trigger/granted-tools.ts:275 is a different gate); the test files operator-confirm-review-tools.test.ts and operator-confirmations.test.ts were read for a case with no allowed list"
        }
      },
      "claimed_disposition": "fixed"
    },
