        "line": 638,
        "quote": "expect(result.output).toContain(\"nothing was recorded\");",
        "problem": "Only the evidence-level gate is proven to record nothing when review_complete is refused. The head gate, waiver rules, run-profile refusal and routing refusal are never driven through the card, and toContain('nothing was recorded') does not identify the gate that refused.",
        "impact": "The point of AC4 is that the card runs the SAME gates as `keryx review complete`. If completeReviewGated drops or reorders a gate on the card path (for example the head gate is skipped, or the refusal is returned after the write), the suite stays green. Only the evidence gate is protected.",
        "suggested_fix": "Table-drive the refused-gate test over each gate with a package that trips only that gate: moved head and merged PR (inject prLookup returning the merged or advanced state; today the helper uses `prLookup: async () => null`, which makes complete-head-gate.ts warn and skip the check), a waiver that breaks the waiver rules, a manifest with the operatorGate stamp so runProfileRefusal fires, and a narrowed routing so packageRoutingRefusal fires. For each: press remote yes, expect isError, expect the gate-specific text, expect completion-confirmation.json absent and the manifest unchanged. Add a small complete-gated.test.ts that asserts the CLI runComplete and the card call the same function.",
        "evidence": "operator-confirm-review.ts line 750 calls completeReviewGated inside apply; src/review/complete-gated.ts holds the four gates; the refused-gate test in operator-confirm-review-tools.test.ts (around line 638) uses only the evidence-level case. The tool() helper's prLookup returns null, and src/review/complete-head-gate.ts line 45 returns a warning and skips the check on a null lookup, so the head gate is inert in these tests.",
        "confidence": "high",
        "class_scope": {
          "sites": [
            "src/commands/operator-confirm-review-tools.test.ts (only the evidence-level refusal is driven)",
            "src/review/complete-head-gate.test.ts (head gate tested directly, not through the card)",
            "src/review/readiness.test.ts (waiver rules tested directly, not through the card)"
          ],
          "enumeration_method": "keryx ctx rg for review_complete across src test files (src/commands/operator-confirm-review-tools.test.ts, src/tui/operator-confirmations.test.ts, src/commands/review-tty-refusal.test.ts) and for each gate name the CLI complete path runs (head, waiver, run-profile, routing, evidence level); only the evidence-level refusal is exercised through the card"
